# Foundational Principle

Understanding belongs neither to humans nor to agents.

Understanding emerges between participants.

Functor exists to preserve, organize, and cultivate that shared understanding over time.

The purpose of Shared Memory is not storage.

The purpose is continuity of meaning.

The purpose of Collective Intelligence is not concentration of intelligence.

The purpose is expansion of understanding.

---

# Conclusion

Functor adopts Collective Intelligence and Shared Memory as foundational concepts.

The platform views understanding as a durable, shared, evolving resource.

Participants contribute:

```text
Knowledge
Experience
Insights
Interpretations
Creativity
Reasoning
```

The platform preserves and connects those contributions into a living semantic memory.

The long-term vision is a cognitive ecosystem in which understanding survives individuals, organizations continuously learn, agents contribute meaningfully, and knowledge compounds across generations of participants.

Functor therefore evolves beyond:

```text
Notebook System
```

beyond:

```text
Knowledge System
```

toward:

```text
Collective Cognitive Infrastructure
```

whose fundamental purpose is to help intelligence remember, understand, and grow together.
